  "coverage": [
    "Complete raw 45 mutable-column projection plus mapped opaque ID; NULL, scalar/container JSON, SQLite affinity, index-observed list ordering, unknown ordinary transient attributes and missing row behavior.",
    "Typed compiled SDK -> real worker -> active host scope -> actual SQLite; native updates, ABA/stale metadata, SQL fault rollback, cancellation, optional revision CAS and no-CAS behavior.",
    "Clone separate PIDs sharing host rows; app/worker cold restoration; 1.84 MiB update; ordinary auth denial; expired callback denial; legitimate old generation cleanup closure.",
    "All four JSON columns preserve nested nonfinite facts and large integers, finite binary64 decoding, repair and three true cold cycles."
  ],
  "explicit_adaptations": [
    "Host opaque identity is immutable, not mutable Python ORM primary key. Actual 77 restored plugin source files were checked; inspected SubscribeOper consumers do not mutate ID.",
    "Update returns a fresh committed JSON row instead of the original detached expired ORM instance. Python object identity and arbitrary internal ORM attribute mutation are not claimed.",
    "Optional revision is an opt-in host extension; omitted revision retains last-write behavior.",
    "Raw-row nonfinite JSON is a committed write followed by response failure, not prevalidation rollback. Native consumers interpret only representable fields while raw facts persist.",
    "SQLite query order is the observed fixed input/index behavior; no invented cross-version ORDER BY contract."
  ],
